{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1485068-mage-the-ascension-traditions-as-nameless-orders","id":1485068,"title":"Mage: The Ascension Traditions as Nameless Orders?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-26T18:19:24-07:00","id":1485068,"title":"Mage: The Ascension Traditions as Nameless Orders?","content":"So, I am running a V5 game where I made mention of the the Order of Hermes being behind the SI's destruction of the Tremere Chantry in Vienna. But I want to use the overall setting of Awakening for this particular V5 game I am running. How would groups like the OOH, the Verbena, or the Sahajiya look as Nameless Orders under the rubric of the Free Council, which supposedly has as large a membership equal to the 4 Diamond orders or the Seers? Has anyone done any work in this direction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T19:55:04-07:00","id":1485073,"title":"","content":"For clarity, by &quot;under the rubric of the Free Council&quot; do you mean &quot;as part of the Free Council&quot;? Because if they're part of the Free Council then they're no longer Nameless Orders \u2014 that was part of the point of the Council of Free Assemblies becoming a (loosely) unified Sect of their own. A Nameless Order is mechanically modeled with most of the same mechanics as Mystery Cult Initiation \u2014 Awakening's version of the Tremere are organized as a Nameless Order that facilitates some of the modifications to their template.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that the Orders being given equally-long writeups doesn't translate to their having equivalent headcount; all the Seers put together number about two thirds of the combined membership of the three Pentacle Orders that aren't the Guardians (smallest major Order in the setting) and the Council (largest major Order in the setting), which nonetheless may translate to equivalent numbers between the Followers of the Lie and their sworn enemies since the line avoids giving hard numbers.<br /> <br /> I'm unfortunately not terribly familiar with Ascension's particulars, but the <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114433/Mage-Translation-Guide\" target=\"_blank\">Mage Translation Guide</a> has some material for translating splats between the two settings that may be useful for your purposes, bearing in mind that it was written back when Awakening was in its late first edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T20:05:57-07:00","id":1485074,"title":"","content":"To add on to Satchel's point, don't mistake &quot;if they're under the umbrella of the Free Council then they're not technically Nameless Orders anymore&quot; for &quot;they've lost their distinct identities and dissolved into the Libertine identity.&quot; The Councillors are a lot less unified in their culture and precepts than the Diamond Orders are, and while they now benefit from sharing rote knowledge and resources amongst each other rather than each internal school having its own distinct Nameless Order Merit benefits, their Order Tool of Techn\u00e9 models a wide breadth of methodologies that still leaves plenty of room for iconoclastic Hermetic Councillors to differ in practices from priests of a pre-Christian craft of blood and life.<br /> <br /> If you want to give them more distinct mechanical identities than that, they would easily make for thematic fodder for Legacies. You can see influences from various Ascension groups in some of Awakening's Legacies already, like the Perfected Adepts drawing on some similar vibes from the Akashic Brotherhood, and the Dreamspeakers resembling... well, I think you can figure that one out pretty quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T13:00:11-07:00","id":1485136,"title":"","content":"If you're willing to set your current approach aside, you can consider implementing Ascension's Traditions as Legacies. Unlike in Ascension, each Order has members who subscribe to varying symbolisms. Not only Free Councillors can model themselves after Verbena - all other Orders can too, just with different goals in mind. Free Councillors will simply be more invested in experiencing Sleeper culture and its non-Supernal aspects, like living together with mundane neo-pagans. This is where Legacies come in. They're &quot;Prestige Classes&quot; that result from Mages internalizing an aspect of Magic to such a degree it becomes a part of their Gnosis. They also form little communities of adherents who can come from multiple Orders - united by common purpose and methodology. As an example, Hermetic aesthetics in Awakening have been relegated to Thrice-Great. They study hermetic symbolism to interact with Spirits of planetary courts. Their membership overlaps mostly with Silver Ladder, who are Mages most likely to be human supremacists, but they can coordinate support from the rest of the Pentacle.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-28T16:57:54-07:00","id":1485229,"title":"","content":"Great notes so far. There's a lot to be said for implementing the Traditions as Legacies. This releases them from the tethers of the Orders and lets them be their own thing. Stand by, I'm going to try to work up the OOH as a Legacy and see what happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-29T02:59:04-07:00","id":1485269,"title":"","content":"I mean, if all you have is a name; the Order of Hermes could be basically anything. Like, maybe the local Viennese caucus of the Silver Ladder calls themselves the Order of Hermes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T22:31:19-07:00","id":1485959,"title":"","content":"Would the Cult of Ecstasy be an Acanthus Legacy, due to the Time Arcana? <br /> <br /> I can't imagine them attracting members from many Orders, aside from the Free Council and some of the more decadent Silver Ladder (maybe the Legacy is where members of those two find some common ground?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T23:18:50-07:00","id":1485961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1485068-mage-the-ascension-traditions-as-nameless-orders?p=1485959#post1485959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would the Cult of Ecstasy be an Acanthus Legacy, due to the Time Arcana? <br /> <br /> I can't imagine them attracting members from many Orders, aside from the Free Council and some of the more decadent Silver Ladder (maybe the Legacy is where members of those two find some common ground?).</div> </div> </div> </div>I see them as a Thyrsus Legacy (since its the Path of Ecstasy) with Time ruling and Spirit optional.<br /> <br /> The Tradition focuses on ecstasy in the sense of self transcendence, hearing the heartbeat of reality by adjusting your perceptions, which then lets you manipulate it. I think that is an apt description for the experience the Watchtower of the Singing Stone can provide. <br /> <br /> Life connects with the physical heart of the world, spirit reveals the emotion and instinct behind it. Time lets you listen to its heartbeat, understand its rhythms. Together they allow the mage to achieve bliss by expanding their perspective, transcending limitations of the mind and body.<br /> <br /> I see them as a Mysterium Legacy. The Order worships magic and you can see a similar focus on expanding one's senses in the ceremonies to advance as an Egregore, as well as the faction's overall methodology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-07-2022, 09:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T06:15:03-07:00","id":1485978,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a>, what sort of Legacy would Dreamspeakers be, then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T06:42:32-07:00","id":1485981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1485068-mage-the-ascension-traditions-as-nameless-orders?p=1485978#post1485978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a>, what sort of Legacy would Dreamspeakers be, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dreamspeakers would be the Dreamspeakers, they already have a fully fleshed Legacy with their name. Its a Thyrsus one with Mind Ruling and Spirit optional, primary of the Free Council, found on page 14 of <i>Legacies: The Ancient</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-16-2022, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T10:28:05-07:00","id":1485990,"title":"","content":"Did the Sons (Society) of Ether get one, too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T11:51:35-07:00","id":1486002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1485068-mage-the-ascension-traditions-as-nameless-orders?p=1485990#post1485990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did the Sons (Society) of Ether get one, too?</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a bit more difficult. The cutting edge scientist torch was passed to the Transhuman Engineers, which can be found in page 118 of <i>Legacies:The Sublime</i>, but I think this <a href=\"https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2016/10/mage-awakening-2nd-edition-legacy.html\" target=\"_blank\">2ed conversion</a> is just fantastic. When looking to create post-human clockwork horror, the Austere would be the ones to focus on. They can be found on page 172 of <i>Guardians of the Veil</i> and a 2ed conversion can be found <a href=\"https://m45t1g05.blogspot.com/2019/09/mage-awakening-2e-legacy-austere.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> However, the community made some amazing technomancy Legacies that I cannot recommend enough. One of my favorites is proindrakenzol's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981289-2e-legacy-thaumatech-engineers\">Thaumatech Engineers</a>, a imbued item focused one that is inspired by the Girl Genius webcomic. If you are looking for mechs and power armor, then GibberingEloquence's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1291687-new-legacy-the-clockwork-knights\">Clockwork Knights</a> are hard to beat, they are also great if you want to make a Doomslayer with his praetor suit. Lastly, I have also made the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1402100-the-anima-meccanica-a-moros-legacy-of-entrepreneuring-inventors\">Anima Meccanica</a>, a solarpunk one focused on integrating spirits into inventions, which was inspired by <i>Prey</i>, the Adeptus Mechanicus, Iron Man and Kaladesh.<br /> <br /> I would also like to mention proindrakenzol's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/889501-2e-legacy-mentats\">Mentats </a>as a candidate for the Virtual Adepts, with 21C Hermit's version of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e?p=1109045#post1109045\">Cloud Infinite</a> (originally found in the <i>Free Council</i> book) being great candidates to create evil tech masterminds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-07-2022, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T13:43:52-07:00","id":1486007,"title":"","content":"Thank you all so far. Ever since reading about the Tremere nameless order in Night Horrors: Nameless and Accursed, I like that Nameless Order format. I'm also considering fooling around with Mystery Cult Initiation Mechanics.<br /> <br /> I generally see groups like the Verbena, The Order of Hermes and the Sahajiya being more regionally focused than the world wide Orders, and politically aligned with the Free Council even if their praxis (and game mechanics) would be different. I like the idea of being Free Council accessible Legacies best, however. Let me start writing and see what happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}